# Goal

Answer Joel's 2026-09-11 #lc-ai-hero ask ("make this nice", wzrrd mockup
`aih-team-flow-2026-09-10-v7n3qk`, "bring team story to the surface") without
disturbing the workshop sidebar pricing widget that is converting today.

# Evidence

- Front: nearly every `/for-your-team` inquiry (Sutter Health, BAC, Reveal AI,
  Loihde, 2026-09-09..10) is answered by Joel with recorded team access to the
  completed cohort "AI Coding for Real Engineers", not the crash course. Larger
  groups get a call-booking link.
- `/courses` "Bringing your team?" banner (`FLAGSHIP_TEAM` in
  `src/lib/courses-content.ts`) is the highest-volume entry and links to
  `/for-your-team`.
- The cohort lives under `/cohorts/[slug]`, a different route family from
  `/workshops/[module]`, so a per-workshop teams page cannot cover it.

# Decisions (grilled 2026-09-11)

1. Workshop sidebar pricing widget stays the individual path. The
   "Buying for your team?" checkbox, stepper and boss-letter card all stay.
2. Entry point (settled after three rounds on 2026-09-11): an outline button
   "Buy for your team" directly under the gold buy button, the primary's
   twin; and a compact "For your team" outline button beside the buy button
   in the mobile bar. The "Buying for your team?" checkbox stays. The small
   row link and the bottom side-link card were both tried and dropped:
   buried and too small. Boss-letter card stays at the card's foot.
3. New route `/workshops/[module]/for-teams`. Copy lives in a new optional
   `fields.forTeamsBody` MDX field on the workshop, exposed in the editor as a
   second "For teams" body (same pattern as cohort `postPurchaseBody`, done as
   a local override on the spread `workshopManifest`; no `@coursebuilder/ui`
   release). The page owns the layout: hero from workshop title, MDX field,
   logo wall, seats section, inquiry form. Empty field returns 404.
4. Seat checkout embeds the existing pricing container in team mode with the
   individual checkbox hidden. No separate seats route.
5. Contact is the existing `TeamInquiryForm` inline, source tagged with the
   workshop slug so Front subjects show the product.
6. Logo wall reuses `CompanyLogoGrid` with its "Trusted by engineers from"
   claim. "Trusted by teams at" is not a claim we can defend.
7. `/for-your-team` stays the generic hub, rebuilt as a two-offer page:
   crash-course team seats (links to the new page) and cohort recordings
   (scrolls to the inquiry form). Courses banner and nav keep pointing here.
8. Delete the unused `TeamPricingWidget` component.
9. One branch, one PR; ngrok preview posted in Joel's thread before merge.

# Out of scope

Sidebar redesign spec (`docs/workshop-landing-sidebar-actions-spec.md`),
a cohort-specific teams page, Kit or Slack hooks for inquiries.

# Done

- 2026-09-11: shipped on `feat/workshop-for-teams` (3 commits). Verified on the
  ngrok dev app: hub, teams page (hero, story, logo wall, seats card in team
  mode pricing 5 seats with the bulk discount, tagged inquiry form), sidebar
  row link plus bottom card. Crash-course `forTeamsBody` pasted by Vojta via
  the dev editor (prod DB; inert until deploy).
- Gotcha: `WORKSHOP_CTA_BUTTON` lived in a `'use client'` module. A string
  imported from one into a server component arrives as a client reference and
  `cn()` drops it silently. It now lives in `workshop-cta-button.ts`.
- Gotcha: the workshop cover is a 16:9 card with the title drawn in; never
  `object-cover` it into a narrow column. The teams hero shows it at its own
  ratio in a balanced split.
- CTA vocabulary: the secondary ask on the team pages is "Get a quote for
  your team" (form), the hub's crash-course card says "See team options"
  (goes to the page), the workshop card says "Buy for your team". Labels
  name what the reader gets, never the act of contacting.
